ts to see this dispute  settled in a proper way but we need Pace  six months we've been negotiating at  least with the train operators and we've  had not one document put across the  table that has to change and I outline  to him what his responsibilities are as  we see them and his responsibilities are  legally in the contracts they have with  these train operators he's got a legal  responsibility for industrial relations  and a responsibility to set their  mandate I.E what they can say what they  can offer and what they can negotiate on  at that table  so I'm hoping he's going to do that  hopefully today and we can get back to  the table as he's been demanded in the  media uh from me and from my union but  he needs to clarify him writing exactly  where he stands and where the industry  stands when they are uh you know  transacting with us in those discussions  so they need a new position they need a  new mandate and hopefully we can get on  with it and we'll be looking to do that  immediately we'll be talking to network  rail in the morning and as soon as the  rail delivery group invite us over we'll  be getting on with that so that's where  we are at the moment it's up to him now  to give us some documentation about how  we're going to carry this forward
 

